.TH TTYCHATTER.NCURSES 1 "November 2026" "ttychatter.ncurses 0.17.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttychatter.ncurses \- full-screen ncurses OpenRouter chat interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttychatter.ncurses
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ session ]
.br
.B ttychatter.ncurses
.BR --list
.br
.B ttychatter.ncurses
.BR --rename-session " SESSION TITLE"
.br
.B ttychatter.ncurses
.BR --turns " SESSION"
.br
.B ttychatter.ncurses
.BR --branch " SESSION TURN"
.br
.B ttychatter.ncurses
.BR --export " SESSION"
.RB [ --format
.IR markdown|text|json ]
.RB [ --output
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ttychatter.ncurses
is the full-screen terminal UI edition. It prioritizes interactive browsing,
model selection, options, attachments, memory inspection, and session management.
It inherits the terminal foreground and background, supports a hideable draft,
and offers a full command menu through Escape, with F1 as an optional alias. List, rename, turns,
branch, and export operations are also available outside the UI.
.SH SESSION LOGS AND TITLES
New logs begin with:
.PP
.nf
Everyone is encouraged to get the cruelty-free vegetarian alternatives and remember the bloodguilt curse from the Bible... http://bloodguiltcurse.net
.fi
.PP
New unnamed interactive sessions ask for a human title. If still unnamed after
the first successful reply, the program asks again. The Escape command menu
contains the naming action. PROMPT_SESSION_NAME=0 disables automatic naming prompts.
.PP
Titles are stored as session-title metadata and appear in the physical log
filename. A named file uses a sanitized title, two hyphens, and the first 12
characters of its stable session-id. Collision suffixes prevent overwriting.
Renaming retains the full title, session ID, old filename and title aliases,
and existing attachment paths. Exact title or alias lookups must be unambiguous.
Explicit --session names initially keep their requested filename. Unnamed logs
keep timestamped filenames until named. Existing logs remain readable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.TP
.B --demo
Use local demo responses and demo model metadata.
.TP
.B --session NAME
Open or create NAME. This is an alias for the positional session operand.
.TP
.B --resume NAME
Resume an existing session.
.TP
.B --new
Force a fresh timestamped session.
.TP
.B --list
List saved sessions with title metadata when present.
.TP
.BR --rename-session " SESSION TITLE"
Set the full human title, safely rename the physical log, and print its new path.
.TP
.BR --turns " SESSION"
List user/assistant message numbers.
.TP
.BR --branch " SESSION TURN"
Create a new timestamped branch containing messages through TURN.
.TP
.BR --edit-turn " SESSION TURN"
Recognized for parity, but not implemented in the ncurses edition. Use the C
edition or ttychatter.python.
.TP
.BR --export " SESSION"
Export a session.
.TP
.BR --format " markdown|text|json"
Choose export format.
.TP
.BR --output " FILE"
Write export output to FILE.
.TP
.B --models
List cached models, fetching the cache if needed.
.TP
.B --routers
List router/special model entries.
.TP
.BR --model-type " all|routers|fixed|free|auto"
Filter model display.
.TP
.B --update-models
Refresh the OpenRouter model cache.
.TP
.B --doctor
Run diagnostics.
.TP
.BR --test-model " MODEL"
Send MODEL_TEST_PROMPT to MODEL and print the response.
.TP
.BR --loopback-file " PATH"
Append each AI response to PATH while the ncurses UI remains interactive.
.TP
.B --stream
Stream assistant output into the transcript. Provider I/O runs outside the curses
event loop, so menus, options, and transcript navigation remain usable while the
stream is active.
.TP
.B --no-stream
Disable streaming for this run even when STREAM=1 is configured.
.TP
.B --web
Enable the OpenRouter web-search server tool for this run. The model decides
whether to search. Search and token charges may apply.
.TP
.B --no-web
Do not add the web-search tool for this run, overriding WEB_SEARCH=1.
.TP
.BR --web-engine " auto|native|exa|parallel|perplexity|firecrawl"
Choose the search engine. The default is auto.
.TP
.BR --web-max-results " N"
Request 0..25 results per search; the default is 5. Zero leaves the provider default. Perplexity is capped at 20 when a nonzero limit is set.
.TP
.BR --web-max-uses " N"
Request 0..25 search rounds per reply; the default is 3. Zero omits ttychatter's max_tool_calls cap. Provider limits still apply. It is not a monetary budget.
.TP
.BR --ai-download " ask|auto|metadata|off"
Control provider-returned file attachments. In ask mode a nonstreaming response
prompts before saving each returned file. During streaming, ask records metadata
only. auto saves returned files under ATTACHMENT_DIR/received, metadata lists
them without saving, and off ignores them. Received files have a 20 MiB size
limit and never overwrite an existing file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The shared config file is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/config
or, when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset,
.IR ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config .
Sessions default to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions ,
attachments to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments ,
and the model cache to
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json .
Model favorites default to
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/model-favorites .
All implementations use these shared paths and still read the old
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/config
file as a compatibility fallback when the provider-specific config is absent.
Relevant keys include MODEL, CONTEXT_TURNS, SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR,
EDITOR, MODEL_CACHE_FILE, MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE, MODEL_FILTER_CHAT_COMPLETIONS,
MODEL_FILTER_REQUIRE_TOKENS, MODEL_FILTER_HIDE_PREVIEW,
MODEL_MIN_INPUT_TOKENS, MODEL_MIN_OUTPUT_TOKENS, MODEL_SORT_ORDER,
MODEL_TYPE_FILTER, THEME, SEND_INPUT, PROMPT_SESSION_NAME, INPUT_HEIGHT,
WEB_SEARCH, WEB_SEARCH_ENGINE, WEB_SEARCH_MODE, WEB_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS, WEB_SEARCH_MAX_USES,
CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES, MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, GITHUB_URL, STARTUP_NOTICE, SESSION_AUTO_TITLE,
SESSION_TITLE_MODEL, SESSION_TITLE_MAX_WORDS, STREAM, AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE, DEMO_MODE,
CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND, API_KEY_GPG_FILE, and LOOPBACK_FILE.
.PP
SESSION_AUTO_TITLE defaults to 0. When enabled, SESSION_TITLE_MODEL generates a
short title after a response and the log is renamed accordingly. The chat model
remains MODEL. Title generation does not enable web search. Manual titles are
not shortened to SESSION_TITLE_MAX_WORDS.
.PP
All legacy THEME values now use the terminal's foreground and background. Bold
and reverse video provide emphasis without a custom palette. INPUT_HEIGHT is
the visible draft height, default 3, range 1..12, constrained by screen size.
.SH KEYBOARD AND LAYOUT
.TP
.B Escape
Open the full scrollable command menu. F1 is an optional alias, so a terminal emulator that consumes F1 does not block access.
.TP
.B F11
Hide or show the draft. Hidden text and cursor position are preserved.
.TP
.B PgUp / PgDn
Scroll the transcript by one visible page.
.TP
.B Up / Down or k / j
In read mode, scroll the transcript one line. With the draft visible, arrow keys edit the draft.
.TP
.B u / d
In read mode, scroll half a page.
.TP
.B g / G
In read mode, go to the oldest or latest transcript position.
.TP
.B F2 / F3 / F4
Models / API key / sessions. The session browser defaults to newest first; s changes sorting, / searches titles, f searches inside log files, and x clears searches.
.TP
.B F5 / F6 / F7
Options / memory / files. Web settings live in Options. Attachment actions live in Files and have no global control-key shortcuts.
.TP
.B F8
Open external-editor options. The editor runs only after selecting Open in external editor.
.TP
.B F9
About / credits.
.TP
.B F10
Close-session confirmation. Only Y exits.
.TP
.B Configured send key
Enter is the default. Ctrl+G is captured only when SEND_INPUT=ctrl_g is explicitly selected.
.PP
Network generation is asynchronous in the ncurses client. Menus, function-key screens, options, and transcript navigation remain usable while a response is in flight. When response text is first rendered, the main chat automatically enters read mode.
.SH WEB SEARCH AND RESPONSE METADATA
WEB_SEARCH defaults to 0. The preferred implementation uses the
openrouter:web_search server tool. No separate search key or local search
process is required. WEB_SEARCH_MODE may be auto, server-tool, or plugin. Auto
uses the agentic server tool when possible and falls back once to OpenRouter's
web plugin when cached model metadata lacks tools or OpenRouter returns the
specific no-tool-capable-endpoint HTTP 404. The plugin performs one pre-answer
search rather than an agentic search loop.
.PP
WEB_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS and WEB_SEARCH_MAX_USES accept 0. Zero results omits an
explicit result limit and leaves the provider default. Zero uses omits
max_tool_calls, meaning ttychatter imposes no search-round cap. Nonzero values
are bounded by ttychatter and provider constraints and are not a dollar budget.
.PP
Supplied source annotations become a Sources section. Response IDs, usage,
provider/model information, annotations, and reasoning details are recorded as
system metadata outside conversation memory. Stream parsing reads final usage
through [DONE] and retains partial text on error. Both streaming and
nonstreaming generation run outside the curses event loop so the UI remains
interactive while the request is in flight.
.PP
Current OpenRouter reference pages:
https://openrouter.ai/tool/web-search/
https://openrouter.ai/blog/agentic-web-tools/
.SH MEMORY AND FILE PRESERVATION
JSON context snapshots preserve multiline entries. Resume loads the latest
complete snapshot plus later real conversation turns. An empty snapshot means
memory was intentionally cleared. Legacy CONTEXT_BEGIN / CONTEXT_END blocks
remain readable. Metadata and the exact project-notice entry are excluded.
.PP
If saving a received answer fails, the raw reply remains in the transcript and
F8 Save last reply to file can recover it. Configuration replacement is atomic.
Extracted code and received attachments reserve new filenames without replacing
earlier files.
.SH SEE ALSO
ttychatter.bash(1), ttychatter.python(1)
